WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.632 --> 00:00:09.054
"Look, Dad!"

2
00:00:09.514 --> 00:00:10.995
Lila said, waving a flyer.

3
00:00:11.915 --> 00:00:15.336
"The amusement park is having a roller coaster design contest.

4
00:00:17.597 --> 00:00:21.898
First prize is two tickets for the first ride on the new coaster!"

5
00:00:23.438 --> 00:00:26.319
Dad leaned back and pretended he was riding a roller coaster.

6
00:00:26.339 --> 00:00:29.000
"I love when I'm pushed back in the seat."

7
00:00:31.532 --> 00:00:33.614
"It only feels like you're being pushed back.

8
00:00:35.415 --> 00:00:37.737
The seat is really pushing you forward."

9
00:00:38.838 --> 00:00:39.479
Dad laughed.

10
00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:42.141
"You sure know your stuff!"

11
00:00:44.323 --> 00:00:45.885
Lila started drawing ideas.

12
00:00:47.346 --> 00:00:48.707
First she drew a lift hill.

13
00:00:50.249 --> 00:00:52.310
She knew that roller coasters didn't have motors.

14
00:00:54.813 --> 00:00:58.416
The cars gained speed as gravity pulled them down from the top of the lift hill.

15
00:01:01.536 --> 00:01:04.637
This momentum would carry the cars through the rest of the roller coaster.

16
00:01:04.657 --> 00:01:09.119
"My hill looks too short," Lila thought.

17
00:01:09.139 --> 00:01:14.782
"The cars won't have enough momentum to go through loops or over hills."

18
00:01:15.722 --> 00:01:17.103
She made the hill a bit taller.

19
00:01:18.183 --> 00:01:21.165
If she made it too tall, the cars would gain too much speed.

20
00:01:22.465 --> 00:01:24.686
Then the ride would be uncomfortable or dangerous.

21
00:01:25.807 --> 00:01:28.908
After the lift hill, Lila added loops, hills, and curves.

22
00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:33.861
"Yes!" Lila declared.

23
00:01:34.341 --> 00:01:36.242
She was almost ready to build a model!

24
00:01:38.584 --> 00:01:41.826
As Dad drove to the park, Lila practiced explaining her model.

25
00:01:41.846 --> 00:01:49.510
"Gravity pulls you down at the top of the loop, but the momentum keeps pushing you forward."

26
00:01:50.951 --> 00:01:52.752
"That gives you the weightless feeling?"

27
00:01:53.032 --> 00:01:53.593
Dad asked.

28
00:01:53.613 --> 00:01:59.336
"Exactly." Dad parked.

29
00:02:00.980 --> 00:02:04.462
As Lila started to get out of the car, the box slipped from her hands.

30
00:02:06.202 --> 00:02:08.903
Lila gasped as her model crashed onto the pavement.

31
00:02:09.484 --> 00:02:11.685
"It's ruined!

32
00:02:12.245 --> 00:02:13.565
What am I going to do?

33
00:02:14.006 --> 00:02:15.406
Judging starts soon!"

34
00:02:16.507 --> 00:02:17.907
Dad helped her pick up the pieces.

35
00:02:17.927 --> 00:02:21.149
"It's not too bad.

36
00:02:21.449 --> 00:02:22.349
You'll think of something."

37
00:02:25.211 --> 00:02:28.292
In the waiting room, Lila examined the other contestants' designs.

38
00:02:29.340 --> 00:02:31.241
Some wouldn't work, but others were good.

39
00:02:32.721 --> 00:02:34.982
She stared at the pieces of her model in the box.

40
00:02:35.002 --> 00:02:37.842
"Hey!" she thought suddenly.

41
00:02:37.862 --> 00:02:42.664
"Maybe I can put the pieces together as I explain my model!"

42
00:02:45.265 --> 00:02:46.485
Soon it was Lila's turn.

43
00:02:46.965 --> 00:02:49.526
In the judging room, Lila put the lift hill on the table.

44
00:02:49.546 --> 00:02:53.747
"A cable pulls the cars to the top."

45
00:02:55.307 --> 00:02:57.108
Next she put the loop on the table.

46
00:02:59.048 --> 00:03:03.411
"From the lift hill, the cars should have enough speed to go through this loop."

47
00:03:03.431 --> 00:03:06.934
"Why isn't the loop round?"

48
00:03:07.354 --> 00:03:08.415
judge number one asked.

49
00:03:08.435 --> 00:03:13.599
"A round loop makes the cars go the same speed all around.

50
00:03:14.900 --> 00:03:20.344
This teardrop shape slows the speed on the sides of the loop to make the ride more comfortable."

51
00:03:22.466 --> 00:03:23.266
The judges nodded.

52
00:03:23.667 --> 00:03:24.928
Lila's plan was working!

53
00:03:26.848 --> 00:03:29.990
But as she took the last piece from the box, her heart sank.

54
00:03:31.151 --> 00:03:33.213
Part of the track was twisted upside down!

55
00:03:33.233 --> 00:03:36.975
"Interesting," judge number two said.

56
00:03:36.995 --> 00:03:41.839
"This isn't how I designed it," Lila admitted.

57
00:03:41.859 --> 00:03:45.101
"I dropped the model in the parking lot."

58
00:03:47.683 --> 00:03:50.665
"Do you think it would work on a real coaster?"

59
00:03:51.086 --> 00:03:52.146
judge number one asked.

60
00:03:52.167 --> 00:03:59.732
"Hmm. I think the momentum coming out of the loop would carry the cars through the twist."

61
00:04:03.714 --> 00:04:05.455
Lila sat nervously in the waiting room.

62
00:04:05.476 --> 00:04:09.118
"I couldn't answer the twist question."

63
00:04:09.138 --> 00:04:12.981
"I'm sure you did well," Dad assured her.

64
00:04:14.321 --> 00:04:16.403
Finally the judges called everyone back in.

65
00:04:16.423 --> 00:04:21.907
"The winner is Lila King!"

66
00:04:22.347 --> 00:04:23.488
judge number one announced.

67
00:04:25.112 --> 00:04:29.793
"For her good model and her great knowledge of roller coaster physics!"

68
00:04:31.314 --> 00:04:34.094
Judge number two shook Lila's hand and handed her the tickets.

69
00:04:38.156 --> 00:04:41.537
company has a summer camp for future engineers," he said.

70
00:04:41.557 --> 00:04:44.577
"You should think about attending."

71
00:04:46.118 --> 00:04:46.778
Lila grinned.

72
00:04:47.798 --> 00:04:53.860
"I'll definitely look into it—after I ride the new coaster!"
